{"availability":"available","full":"binwiederhier/pcopy","name":"pcopy","description":"pcopy is a temporary file host, nopaste and clipboard across machines. It can be used from the Web UI, via a CLI or without a client by using curl.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":425,"forks":33,"created":"2020-12-01T14:32:40Z","updated":"2024-04-04T22:59:01Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://nopaste.net","topics":["clipboard","copy-paste","curl","golang","netcat","nopaste","pastebin","self-hosted"],"demo":"https://nopaste.net/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.502Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.502Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.502Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.502Z","stars":425,"forks":33}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pcopy is a tool to copy/paste across machines. It can be used from the web UI, via a CLI or without a client by using curl. It can also be used as a self-hosted NoPaste or as a temporary file hosting service.","After installing the pcopy server, you can use the pcopy command line tool to copy from STDIN (pcp file.txt). If you don't have pcopy installed, you can also use its super simple REST API to copy/paste, e.g. via curl.","The web UI allows you to paste text or upload files (even if they are gigabytes in size), and generates temporary links you can share with others."],"features":["📋 Copy/paste across computers (via STDIN/STDOUT)","🔒 HTTPS secure server (via cert-pinning)","🔑 Clipboards can be password-protected, or they can be open for everyone","📚 Support for multiple clipboards (e.g. personal, work, ...)","🌎 Simple Web UI for uploading text snippets or large files"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/binwiederhier/pcopy/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"52ba5a557b1abceebd65c1ff3b98b3490c203811c9f1abf6b2ab673b4fcd0de0","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.611Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:17.611Z